governor turn 1: ask  ("Easier to read" doesn't give me anything I can test, and I can't see the current output format. Any change to how todos are rendered will probably also break the existing format tests, so I need to know which behaviour you actually want to change before I approve that.)
governor asks: I can't turn "easier to read" into something testable yet. Which of these do you want? Pick any combination, or describe your own.
1. Status markers: show "[x]" for done items and "[ ]" for open ones.
2. Aligned columns: pad the IDs so titles line up, e.g. " 1. [ ] Buy milk" and "10. [x] Pay rent".
3. Due dates: show them in a consistent way, e.g. "(due 2024-05-01)" at the end of the line. Should overdue items be marked?
4. Empty list: show a message like "No todos." instead of printing nothing.
5. Summary: add a footer like "3 open, 2 done".
6. Colour: use ANSI colours, e.g. dim done items and red for overdue ones. Is that OK for your terminal, or should the output stay plain text?
Also, should the list put open items before done ones, or keep them in ID order?

